

Implement one small change in the existing
TestNG lifecycle listener.

When beforeInvocation(TEST) resolves the
INVOCATION context, store its UUID as a
dedicated attribute on the TEST's ITestResult.

Requirements:
1. Use a unique attribute name.
2. Do not reuse ACTIVATION_ATTRIBUTE.
3. Keep the UUID after afterInvocation(TEST).
4. Do not store context objects or mutable
   configuration objects in the result.
5. Do not change teardown completion logic.
6. Preserve existing lifecycle behavior.

Add real TestNG 7.12.0 integration tests verifying:

- onTestSuccess receives the INVOCATION UUID
  through its ITestResult.
- It matches the UUID from the test body.
- Two consecutive invocations have distinct UUIDs.
- Parallel invocations never share or confuse UUIDs.

Do not modify unrelated production components.
Do not weaken existing assertions.

Run the relevant integration tests and report
the results.

